\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.1}Problem Setup and Unified Time-Series-to-Language Formulation}{4}{subsection.3.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:unified-formulation}{{3.1}{4}{Problem Setup and Unified Time-Series-to-Language Formulation}{subsection.3.1}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {3.2}Dual-View Native Time-Series Prompting}{4}{subsection.3.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Overview of the proposed framework. Given a raw time series, we construct dual-view native time-series prompts using a temporal branch and a visual branch. The fused soft tokens are projected into the hidden space of a pretrained causal LLM and combined with textual prompts for autoregressive generation; during few-shot adaptation, the language side can be lightly updated with LoRA adapters. Training proceeds through Stage I dual-view self-supervised representation learning and Stage II time-series question answering transfer, with an optional Stage III semantic-bridging and caption-specialization continuation. For downstream few-shot classification, we introduce dataset-specific class tokens and score candidate label sequences in the label subspace. }}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{5}{Overview of the proposed framework. Given a raw time series, we construct dual-view native time-series prompts using a temporal branch and a visual branch. The fused soft tokens are projected into the hidden space of a pretrained causal LLM and combined with textual prompts for autoregressive generation; during few-shot adaptation, the language side can be lightly updated with LoRA adapters. Training proceeds through Stage I dual-view self-supervised representation learning and Stage II time-series question answering transfer, with an optional Stage III semantic-bridging and caption-specialization continuation. For downstream few-shot classification, we introduce dataset-specific class tokens and score candidate label sequences in the label subspace}{figure.1}{}}
